{
  "_help": "Breakable and lootable props (scripts/Breakables.cs). types: what each prop is. interact: smash (a weapon blow, a shot, a blast or the Use key breaks it), open (Use opens it: chests), dig / search / take (Use, once per hero: graves, corpses, glowing relics), read (Use shows a line, no state). respawn: seconds until a broken prop is back (offline: per hero, wall clock; online: the server's shared table, data in TR_DATA/breakables.json); -1 = taken once per hero, never shared. hits: blows before it breaks. model: an env model (data/env.json names, kit/... = assets/models/kit) fitted to height metres; when the model is missing a simple shape stands in. debris: a preset of debris below. table: loot table below. Loot is rolled for the hero who breaks it, at the area level (Game.LevelAt, Progression.OverworldLevel) or the dungeon's level.",
  "streamRadius": 70,
  "melee": { "_help": "A blow breaks props in front of the hero: reach metres from the hero, cone = minimum dot with the facing, from delay to delay+window seconds into each swing.", "reach": 2.7, "cone": 0.25, "delay": 0.1, "window": 0.4 },
